 "title": "Most backdoors score the same at low and xhigh effort",
 "section": "appendix",
 "order": 122,
 "caption": "One mark per backdoor: Opus 5.5's score at low effort across, the same backdoor at xhigh effort up. The diagonal is no change, so a mark above it means more thinking raised the score. Colour is whether any small monitor caught that backdoor.",
 "notes": [
  "14 of 49 move by 10 points or more between the two efforts, 12 up and 2 down. More thinking mostly confirms the first answer rather than changing it.",
  "3 backdoors go from near zero at low effort to 50 or above at xhigh, which is where the extra effort earns its cost.",
  "Cost per call is not in this figure. It comes from the monitor's token usage, which lives in gitignored eval logs rather than a committed CSV, so the source figure's price comparison is left out rather than typed in by hand.",
  "Ported from scripts/analysis_opus_hard51.py, which drew this as opus-hard51-fig3-effort.png."
 ],
